| Finding | Remediation | Where |
|---|---|---|
| B1 the gate ran before the owner's approval of the composites | The order is restored: the composites were re-captured after these fixes and posted; the gate re-ran only once `parity/notes.md` recorded the owner's approval (given 2026-10-29 on the re-captured composites) | `evidence/C36/parity/notes.md` |
| R1 unknown coverage became an all-clear | The card's last line states only what the read established: a missing or failed chart says "Sessions chart not read · figure may be low", an unknown violating count "Activity unknown…", a failed Gateway usage read "Usage not read · <workspace>", an unknown error count "Error count unknown · <workspace>"; "No detections" and "No requests" appear only when the counts are known. Test: "never turns unknown coverage into an all-clear…" | `home.tsx`, `copy.ts`, `home.test.tsx` |
| R2 coverage shown as a request figure without a workspace | The Gateway card without a selected workspace shows an em dash under "requests · today" and names the gate ("No Gateway workspace chosen · choose one in Administration"); the coverage fallback is reserved for the products the core reads without figures, whose metric says "sources read". Test: the same test's last step | `home.tsx`, `copy.ts` |
| R3 "Test a prompt" did not open the Playground | The quick action's arrival names the Runtime product and its `playground` tab, which Administration selects (C35's consumed-once arrival), including after another Runtime tab was chosen. Test: "\"Test a prompt\" opens the Runtime Playground tab itself…" asserts the destination tab | `home.tsx`, `home.test.tsx` |
| R4 severity words missing from attention rows (I9) | Each row's second line starts with the severity word (Critical / Warning / Info) in the severity colour beside the icon tile. Test: "names the severity of each attention row in words…"; the native check records the word in the accessibility tree | `home.tsx`, `acceptance_c36.py` |
| R5 / E1 / E2 the native script could pass with checks skipped | Every mandatory step is observed or fails: the keyboard walk runs while the attention row is populated and must reach its Acknowledge and Snooze controls; Snooze must announce the core's return time and remove the row, the Inbox's Unsnooze brings it back, then Acknowledge removes it; all four quick actions must open their destinations (the Playground tab for "Test a prompt", the Harness, the API Client, Academy); each layout row reads its geometry from the tree it saves, distinguishing the WebView area from the viewport (scroll area), which must be 900×600 at 200% | `acceptance_c36.py` |
